# The checks a pull request waits for before it merges, one "Workflow / job" per line. The landing
# script reads this file from the pull request's base commit, so a pull request can't change its
# own gates. Every check named here must succeed; the others are reported but not waited for.
#
# The code scanning jobs aren't listed: they skip pull requests that change only documentation or
# images, and a check that is named here but never starts blocks the merge. Their findings appear
# under the repository's code scanning alerts.
CI / check
CI / check-linux
CI / check-windows
